    "details": "The primary types of veneers include porcelain, composite resin, and ultra-thin no-prep options like Lumineers. Porcelain veneers are durable and lifelike, composite veneers are more budget-friendly and can be done in one visit, and no-prep veneers require minimal enamel removal, preserving more of the natural tooth structure."
