    "details": "Dental veneers are thin shells that cover the front of your teeth to hide chips, stains, or gaps. Porcelain veneers are durable and resist stains, lasting 10\u201315 years or more, while composite (resin) veneers are thinner and less expensive but have a shorter lifespan and may stain or chip sooner."
